{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Take you Joshua son of Nun.</b> The expression 'for yourself' means: investigate him yourself, and you know him — he is worthy to receive the reward of his attendance, that he never departed from within the tent. This is what King Solomon, peace be upon him, said (Proverbs 27:18): ״נוצר תאנה יאכל פריה״." "<b>A man in whom is spirit.</b> As its Targum renders. And the Rabbis, of blessed memory, interpreted it: that he is able to go against the spirit of each and every one." "<b>And lay your hand upon him.</b> So that Israel may see that he is in his place. And the Rabbis, of blessed memory, interpreted: give him an interpreter (turgeman), and let him expound in your lifetime, so that they should not say of him: he had no business lifting his head in the days of Moses."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:36:33.961060872Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}